    <div type="collection" xml:id="hymnary-oldest-pd">
      <div type="hymn" xml:id="occ-at-bethlehem">
        <head type="title">At Bethlehem</head>
        <note type="author">Clark, Luella</note>
        <note type="hymnal">The Service of Praise</note>
        <note type="edition">1900</note>
        <lg type="stanza" n="1"><l>A Babe in the manger,</l><l>A song in the sky;</l><l>On earth benediction,</l><l>Rejoicing on high.</l><l>A glory for Judah,</l><l>A wonderful Light,</l><l>To lighten the Gentiles</l><l>In sorrow and night.</l></lg>
        <lg type="refrain"><label>Refrain</label><l>A Babe in the manger,</l><l>A song in the sky;</l><l>On earth benediction,</l><l>Rejoicing on high.</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="2"><l>A Prince and a Saviour,</l><l>Immanuel, King;</l><l>An unfailing kingdom</l><l>Of blessing to bring.</l><l>A kingdom of mercy,</l><l>Of love, and of peace,</l><l>Whose power shall ever</l><l>And ever increase.</l></lg>
        <lg type="refrain-marker"><label>[Refrain]</label></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="3"><l>Glad dayspring from Heaven,</l><l>Break bright on our night;</l><l>For morning bring gladness,</l><l>For darkness give light.</l><l>Hail, Son of the Highest,</l><l>Redeemer divine;</l><l>Heav’n’s hosts are thy heralds,</l><l>The star is thy sign.</l></lg>
        <lg type="refrain-marker"><label>[Refrain]</label></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="4"><l>Prepared is thy pathway,</l><l>In passion of pain;</l><l>Eternal thy glory,</l><l>Eternal thy reign.</l><l>Priest, Prophet and Saviour;</l><l>Sing, hosts of the sky,</l><l>Shine, stars, at your brightest;</l><l>Redemption is nigh.</l></lg>
        <lg type="refrain-marker"><label>[Refrain]</label></lg>
      </div>
      <div type="hymn" xml:id="occ-babe-born">
        <head type="title">A Babe Is Born In Bethlehem</head>
        <note type="author">Grundtvig, N. F. S. (Nicolai Frederik Severin), 1783-1872; Aaberg, J. C. (Jens Christian), 1877-1970</note>
        <note type="author-birth">1783; 1877</note>
        <note type="author-death">1872; 1970</note>
        <note type="hymnal">Hymnal for Church and Home</note>
        <note type="edition">1927</note>
        <lg type="stanza" n="1"><l>A Babe is born in Bethlehem,</l><l>Bethlehem,</l><l>Rejoice, rejoice, Jerusalem,</l><l>Hallelujah, hallelujah.</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="2"><l>A lowly virgin gave Him birth,</l><l>Gave Him birth,</l><l>Who rules the heavens and the earth,</l><l>Hallelujah, hallelujah.</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="3"><l>He in a simple manger lay,</l><l>Manger lay,</l><l>Whom angels praise with joy for aye.</l><l>Hallelujah, hallelujah.</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="4"><l>And wise men from the East did bring,</l><l>East did bring,</l><l>Gold, myrrh, and incense to the king.</l><l>Hallelujah, hallelujah.</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="5"><l>Now all our fears have pass'd away,</l><l>Passed away,</l><l>The Savior blest was born today.</l><l>Hallelujah, hallelujah.</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="6"><l>God’s blessed children we became,</l><l>We became,</l><l>And shall in heaven praise His name.</l><l>Hallelujah, hallelujah.</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="7"><l>Then like the angels we shall be,</l><l>We shall be,</l><l>God's holy presence we shall see,</l><l>Hallelujah, hallelujah.</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="8"><l>The angels there with great delight,</l><l>Great delight,</l><l>Will teach the song they sang this night.</l><l>Hallelujah, hallelujah.</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="9"><l>With gladsome praises we adore,</l><l>We adore,</l><l>Our Lord and Savior evermore,</l><l>Hallelujah, hallelujah.</l></lg>
      </div>
      <div type="hymn" xml:id="occ-krauth-babe">
        <head type="title">A Babe is born in Bethlehem</head>
        <note type="author">Krauth, C.  P. (Charles Porterfield), 1823-1883</note>
        <note type="author-birth">1823</note>
        <note type="author-death">1883</note>
        <note type="year-written">1869</note>
        <note type="hymnal">Christian Hymns: for church, school and home, with music</note>
        <note type="edition">1898</note>
        <lg type="stanza" n="1"><l>A Babe is born in Bethlehem,</l><l>In Bethlehem,</l><l>Therefore rejoice, Jerusalem.</l><l>Hallelujah, Hallelujah!</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="2"><l>He doth within a manger lie,</l><l>A manger lie,</l><l>Whose throne is set above the sky.</l><l>Hallelujah, Hallelujah!</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="3"><l>Stillness was all the manger round,</l><l>The manger round,</l><l>The creature its Creator found.</l><l>Hallelujah, Hallelujah!</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="4"><l>The wise men came, led by the star,</l><l>Led by the star,</l><l>Gold, myrrh, and incense, brought from far.</l><l>Hallelujah, Hallelujah!</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="5"><l>His mother is the Virgin mild,</l><l>The Virgin mild,</l><l>And He the Father’s only Child.</l><l>Hallelujah, Hallelujah!</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="6"><l>The serpent’s wound He beareth not,</l><l>He beareth not,</l><l>Yet takes our blood, and shares our lot.</l><l>Hallelujah, Hallelujah!</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="7"><l>Our human flesh He enters in,</l><l>He enters in,</l><l>But bears no single taint of sin.</l><l>Hallelujah, Hallelujah!</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="8"><l>To fallen man Himself He bowed,</l><l>Himself He bowed,</l><l>That He might lift us up to God.</l><l>Hallelujah, Hallelujah!</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="9"><l>On this most blessed Jubilee,</l><l>Best jubilee,</l><l>All glory be, O God, to Thee.</l><l>Hallelujah, Hallelujah!</l></lg>
        <lg type="stanza" n="10"><l>O Holy Three, we Thee adore,</l><l>We Thee adore,</l><l>This day, henceforth, for evermore.</l><l>Hallelujah, Hallelujah!</l></lg>
      </div>
    </div>
